usage: latte-bx <command> [options] <file.bx>...

commands:
  build       compile each file, writing <stem>_gen.b beside it
  check       parse and emit, and write nothing
  vocabulary  print latte's .bx surface as JSON, for an editor

options:
  -o <path>          write the generated Beans to <path> (one input only)
  --stdout           write the generated Beans to stdout
  --latte <module>   the module Builder comes from (default: latte)
  --package <name>   the package the generated file declares

A generated file is checked in beside its source, and a drift gate
regenerates and diffs it, so a stale one fails the build rather than
shipping.
